# Boxes only

<small>Genuary 2026, day 12 — prompt by Stranger in the Q</small>

<VideoLoop src="/12/loop.mp4" poster="/12/poster.jpg" label="A large box repeatedly splitting into four smaller boxes that tumble around" />

One box. Click it (or anywhere) and it splits into four quarter-size boxes that
inherit their parent's velocity and tint, get kicked outwards, and tumble around
a zero-gravity room until they are too small to split. Nothing on screen but
axis-misaligned rectangles — boxes only. Each run picks one of eight dark/bright
palettes and every child box drifts a few percent away from its parent's color,
so the swarm slowly becomes a texture.

```kotlin
fun splitBox(box: Box) {
    val newSize = box.size / 2.0
    world.destroyBody(box.body)
    for (localOffset in quadrantOffsets(newSize)) {
        val rotatedOffset = localOffset.rotatedBy(box.body.angle)
        val newBox = createBox(centerPos + rotatedOffset, newSize, tintColor(box.color))
        newBox.body.applyLinearImpulse(rotatedOffset.normalized * randomForce(), newBox.body.worldCenter)
        newBox.body.linearVelocity = box.body.linearVelocity * 0.5f
    }
}
```

